Test fixtures
-------------

The fixtures are in tests/fixtures/office and are not packaged with the
crate.

- sheets/sample.numbers is numbers-parser's tests/data/issue-18.numbers (MIT,
  as above); see sheets/README.md.

- sheets/numbers09.numbers is Apache Tika's test document
  testNumbers.numbers, unmodified, under the Apache License 2.0
  (https://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0). Apache Tika, Copyright The
  Apache Software Foundation; it includes software developed at The Apache
  Software Foundation (http://www.apache.org/). It is a test input only.

- slides/sample.key is keynote-parser's tests/data/simple-oneslide.key, under
  the same licence as keynote-parser above.

- draw/make_vsdx.py writes sample.vsdx and themed.vsdx, Visio drawings of
  shapes written for this crate (CC0); see draw/README.md.

- docs/make.py writes sample.odt, sample.fodt and sample.rtf from text
  written for this crate (CC0). docs/sample.doc is a conversion
  of sample.odt by an office application, and docs/sample-2003.xml was written by hand; none holds
  anyone else's content.

- tests/fixtures/dwg/make.py writes the drawings as DXF with ezdxf (MIT,
  not distributed). The `.dwg.gz` files are those drawings converted to DWG by
  the Open Design Alliance's ODA File Converter, run as a black box on the
  maintainers' machines: no code or data of the converter is in the repository,
  and the drawings are this crate's own, written for the tests and under its
  licence. The converter's own terms
  (https://www.opendesign.com) apply to the converter, not to the files it was
  given. The DWG files carry the file-format markers ODA's writer puts in every
  file.
